    <div class="disclaimer">
      <strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This is an <strong>unofficial navigation resource</strong>. It is not legal advice, not certification, not an official EU publication, and not endorsed by any government body. Official sources always prevail. Always refer to EUR-Lex, eudi.dev, and official EU repositories for authoritative texts.
    </div>

    <div style="max-width: 700px;">

      <div class="detail-section">
        <h3>What is this</h3>
        <p style="font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
          The EUDI Trust & Conformance Atlas is an open, community-maintained map of:
        </p>
        <ul style="font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 2; padding-left: var(--space-5);">
          <li>EUDI Wallet law and implementing acts</li>
          <li>Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) requirements</li>
          <li>WE BUILD trust work and conformance scenarios</li>
          <li>Credimi conformance-evidence mappings</li>
          <li>Trust infrastructure, certification, and assurance references</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-section">
        <h3>Who maintains this</h3>
        <p style="font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.7;">
          Lightly maintained by <strong>Credimi / Forkbomb BV</strong> (Amsterdam, the Netherlands) under the <strong>NGI TRUSTCHAIN</strong> programme.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.7; margin-top: var(--space-2);">
          Credimi uses this map to structure its conformance-evidence profiles, but the data and documentation are published as an open resource for the ecosystem. The site is designed to be useful independently of Credimi.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-section">
        <h3>Important language</h3>
        <p style="font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">
          We use specific language to be precise about what this resource does and does not do:
        </p>
        <dl style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4); font-size: var(--fs-sm);">
          <dt style="color: var(--success);">Use:</dt>
          <dd>"maps to", "relates to", "evidence claim", "supports assurance", "unofficial navigation resource"</dd>
          <dt style="color: var(--destructive);">Avoid:</dt>
          <dd>"certifies", "guarantees conformity", "proves compliance", "official"</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>

